SYNTHESIS "### Technical Synthesis of the July 2025 Siemens SINUMERIK ONE Universal Operating Manual (V6.25 SP1)\n\n#### 1. Warranty and Liability for Application Examples (C01)\n- **Section 2.2 (PDF Page 24)**: Application examples provided in the manual are not binding and do not claim to be comprehensive. They are intended to provide assistance but are not customer-specific solutions.\n\n#### 2. Sidescreen with Standard Windows (C02)\n- **Section (PDF Page 74)**: The sidescreen, when activated, displays a navigation bar on the left-hand side of the user interface. This bar includes controls to switch to different operating areas, such as \"Machine Operating Area\" and \"Tool List.\"\n\n#### 3. Monitoring Axis and Spindle Data (C03)\n- **Section 5.6 (PDF Page 107)**: The \"Working area limitation\" function allows users to set up protection zones in the working area, restricting tool motion within specified ranges. This function helps in setting up safety zones.\n\n#### 4. Opening a DXF File (C04)\n- **Section 7.17.2.1 (PDF Page 191)**: To open a DXF file, users must:\n  1. Select the \"Program Manager\" operating area.\n  2. Choose the desired storage location and position the cursor on the DXF file.\n  3. Press the \"Open\" softkey to display the CAD drawing.\n  4. Press the \"Close\" softkey to close the file.\n\n#### 5. Mold Making View (C05)\n- **Section 7.18 (PDF Pages 202-210)**: The mold making view provides a fast overview of large mold making programs, allowing for quick checking and correction. This view might be hidden, and users should refer to the machine manufacturer's information.\n\n#### 6. Relocating a Tool (C06)\n- **Section 12.8.2 (PDF Page 297)**: To relocate a tool:\n  1. Open the \"Parameter\" operating area.\n  2. Press the \"Magazine\" softkey to open the magazine list.\n  3. Position"
